---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import BackLink from "../../components/BackLink.astro";
---

<Layout
	lang="en"
	title="Private AI for businesses: what it is, why it matters, and how to implement it — Zaviren"
	description="What private AI is, why it protects your business's competitive moat and data, how it's implemented with a dedicated server in your own offices, and how it differs from ChatGPT. A practical guide."
	altHref="/ia-privada"
>
	<section class="hero">
		<span class="eyebrow">Practical guide</span>
		<h1>Private AI <span class="gradient">for businesses</span></h1>
		<p class="subtitle">
			What it is, how it works on your own documents, and how it differs
			from using ChatGPT or Copilot directly.
		</p>
		<div class="cta-row">
			<a class="cta" href="/en/contact">Tell us about your case</a>
			<a class="cta cta-secondary" href="/en/guide">Download the free guide</a>
		</div>
		<div class="hero-illustration">
			<img src="/images/secure-server.svg" alt="Person protecting their own server with a shield" width="400" height="262" />
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="block">
		<div class="block-head">
			<span class="eyebrow">01 · Definition</span>
			<h2>What is <span class="gradient">private AI</span>?</h2>
			<p>
				An AI assistant that answers using your company's documents — but
				runs inside your own infrastructure, without sending anything to a
				third party.
			</p>
		</div>
		<div class="risk-grid">
			<div class="card">
				<h3>Answers with your documents</h3>
				<p>Manuals, contracts, policies, quotes — the answer comes from there, not from the model's generic memory.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="card">
				<h3>RAG: searches before answering</h3>
				<p>It first retrieves the relevant passages from your documents, then writes the answer from them.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="card">
				<h3>Cites the source, doesn't improvise</h3>
				<p>Every answer is anchored to an actual document from your company, not to whatever the model learned during training.</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="block">
		<div class="block-head">
			<span class="eyebrow">02 · Why it matters</span>
			<h2>Why your business <span class="gradient">needs private AI</span></h2>
			<p>
				It's not just a technical choice — it's protecting what makes your
				business competitive.
			</p>
		</div>
		<div class="risk-grid">
			<div class="card">
				<h3>Protects your competitive moat</h3>
				<p>
					Your processes, your contracts, the way you solve problems — that's
					what sets you apart. If every query about that knowledge goes
					through an external provider's cloud, you depend on their
					infrastructure and their data-use policy for something that should
					be exclusively yours.
				</p>
			</div>
			<div class="card">
				<h3>Real privacy and confidentiality</h3>
				<p>
					Payroll, customer data, intellectual property, ongoing negotiations:
					if a cloud provider ever has a breach, the legal and reputational
					risk is yours, not theirs. With your own perimeter, you decide who
					has access, and it's logged.
				</p>
			</div>
			<div class="card">
				<h3>The cost of waiting</h3>
				<p>
					While you evaluate whether it's worth it, competitors who already
					adopted AI well are pulling ahead in response speed and in how they
					leverage their own internal knowledge. That gap gets harder to
					close the longer you wait.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="block">
		<div class="block-head">
			<span class="eyebrow">03 · How it works</span>
			<h2>From question <span class="gradient">to cited answer</span></h2>
		</div>
		<div class="cap-grid">
			<div class="card">
				<span class="cap-num">01</span>
				<div>
					<h3>Your documents, indexed</h3>
					<p>Manuals, contracts and policies are processed once and become searchable in plain language.</p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="card">
				<span class="cap-num">02</span>
				<div>
					<h3>Retrieval of the relevant passage</h3>
					<p>For every question, the system finds which fragments of which documents contain the answer.</p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="card">
				<span class="cap-num">03</span>
				<div>
					<h3>The model writes, without inventing</h3>
					<p>The answer is generated from those specific fragments, citing the document and page.</p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="card">
				<span class="cap-num">04</span>
				<div>
					<h3>All inside your perimeter</h3>
					<p>Documents, search and model run on your infrastructure — nothing leaves to a third party's cloud.</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="block">
		<div class="split">
			<div class="copy">
				<span class="eyebrow">04 · Implementation</span>
				<h2>A dedicated server <span class="gradient">in your own offices</span></h2>
				<p>
					In practice, private AI lives on a physical machine (or a small
					cluster, depending on volume) connected to your internal network —
					inside your office or your own datacenter. It's not another
					provider's cloud account with more locks on it: it's hardware you
					control.
				</p>
				<p>
					That server hosts the language model, the search over your
					documents, and all the orchestration between them. Your employees'
					questions never leave your network — not for training, not for
					querying.
				</p>
			</div>
			<div class="illustration">
				<svg viewBox="0 0 160 160" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
					<defs>
						<linearGradient id="implGradEn" x1="0" y1="0" x2="160" y2="160" gradientUnits="userSpaceOnUse">
							<stop offset="0" stop-color="#3b82f6" />
							<stop offset="1" stop-color="#8b5cf6" />
						</linearGradient>
					</defs>
					<rect x="30" y="20" width="100" height="120" rx="12" stroke="url(#implGradEn)" stroke-width="2" fill="#ffffff08" />
					<rect x="42" y="38" width="76" height="14" rx="4" fill="url(#implGradEn)" opacity="0.6" />
					<rect x="42" y="60" width="76" height="14" rx="4" fill="url(#implGradEn)" opacity="0.4" />
					<rect x="42" y="82" width="76" height="14" rx="4" fill="url(#implGradEn)" opacity="0.25" />
					<circle cx="112" cy="112" r="4" fill="url(#implGradEn)" />
					<circle cx="112" cy="128" r="4" fill="url(#implGradEn)" opacity="0.6" />
				</svg>
			</div>
		</div>
		<div class="risk-grid cols-2">
			<div class="card">
				<h3>Sized to fit</h3>
				<p>Hardware is calculated based on your document volume and concurrent users — never over- or under-sized.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="card">
				<h3>On top of your current storage</h3>
				<p>Connects to the folders, intranet or document manager you already use — no need to migrate anything to get started.</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="block">
		<div class="block-head">
			<span class="eyebrow">05 · Advantages</span>
			<h2>What you gain <span class="gradient">with private AI</span></h2>
		</div>
		<div class="cap-grid">
			<div class="card">
				<span class="cap-num">01</span>
				<div>
					<h3>Full control of your data</h3>
					<p>It never leaves your perimeter, whether for answering or for training anything.</p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="card">
				<span class="cap-num">02</span>
				<div>
					<h3>Protects your competitive edge</h3>
					<p>Your internal knowledge never feeds or gets exposed to a third party's infrastructure.</p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="card">
				<span class="cap-num">03</span>
				<div>
					<h3>Native GDPR compliance</h3>
					<p>No third-party transfer to audit — it fits by default, not as a patch.</p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="card">
				<span class="cap-num">04</span>
				<div>
					<h3>Predictable cost</h3>
					<p>No variable bill per token or per call to an external API that grows with your adoption.</p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="card">
				<span class="cap-num">05</span>
				<div>
					<h3>Works without depending on the internet</h3>
					<p>Once deployed, it runs inside your network — not dependent on an external service's uptime.</p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="card">
				<span class="cap-num">06</span>
				<div>
					<h3>Traceable and auditable</h3>
					<p>Every answer cites its source document and page — you know exactly where each piece of data came from.</p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="card">
				<span class="cap-num">07</span>
				<div>
					<h3>Scales with you</h3>
					<p>The same server covers more use cases as adoption grows across the company.</p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="card">
				<span class="cap-num">08</span>
				<div>
					<h3>No intellectual property leakage</h3>
					<p>Contracts, quotes and proprietary processes never pass through a model you don't control.</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="block">
		<div class="block-head">
			<span class="eyebrow">06 · Comparison</span>
			<h2>Private AI <span class="gradient">vs ChatGPT</span></h2>
			<p>ChatGPT, Copilot and similar tools are excellent generalist assistants — but they weren't built to answer using your company's internal, confidential knowledge.</p>
		</div>
		<div class="compare-grid">
			<div class="compare-row compare-header">
				<span></span>
				<span>ChatGPT / generic AI</span>
				<span>Private AI (Zaviren)</span>
			</div>
			<div class="compare-row">
				<span class="compare-label">Where your data lives</span>
				<span data-label="ChatGPT / generic AI">Sent to the provider's servers</span>
				<span data-label="Zaviren">Stays inside your infrastructure</span>
			</div>
			<div class="compare-row">
				<span class="compare-label">Knows your documents</span>
				<span data-label="ChatGPT / generic AI">No, unless you paste them in manually</span>
				<span data-label="Zaviren">Yes, indexed and always available</span>
			</div>
			<div class="compare-row">
				<span class="compare-label">Cites the exact source</span>
				<span data-label="ChatGPT / generic AI">Rarely, and with no guarantee</span>
				<span data-label="Zaviren">Yes — document and page on every answer</span>
			</div>
			<div class="compare-row">
				<span class="compare-label">GDPR</span>
				<span data-label="ChatGPT / generic AI">Depends on the provider's policy</span>
				<span data-label="Zaviren">Native — no third-party transfer to audit</span>
			</div>
			<div class="compare-row">
				<span class="compare-label">Hallucination risk</span>
				<span data-label="ChatGPT / generic AI">High on topics specific to your company</span>
				<span data-label="Zaviren">Low — answers only with what it finds in your documents</span>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="block">
		<div class="block-head">
			<span class="eyebrow">07 · FAQ</span>
			<h2>Before you <span class="gradient">ask</span></h2>
		</div>
		<div class="faq-list">
			<details class="faq-item">
				<summary>Is this the same as using ChatGPT Enterprise or Microsoft Copilot?</summary>
				<p>No. Those tools still process your data in the provider's cloud, even under enterprise contracts. Private AI runs both the model and the search inside your own infrastructure — there's no data transfer to a third party at any point.</p>
			</details>
			<details class="faq-item">
				<summary>Do I need powerful servers of my own?</summary>
				<p>It depends on document volume and concurrent users. A pilot with a few hundred documents runs on moderate hardware, no dedicated GPU required. We size the exact hardware for your case before starting.</p>
			</details>
			<details class="faq-item">
				<summary>Where exactly does the server get installed?</summary>
				<p>Inside your network — in your own offices or your datacenter if you already have one. It's not a virtual machine in a third party's cloud with extra locks on it: it's physical hardware under your control, connected only to your internal infrastructure.</p>
			</details>
			<details class="faq-item">
				<summary>Does it stop working if the internet goes down?</summary>
				<p>No, once deployed. The model and the search run inside your local network, so availability depends on your own infrastructure, not on an external service.</p>
			</details>
			<details class="faq-item">
				<summary>Is it slower or worse than ChatGPT?</summary>
				<p>For general knowledge questions, it doesn't compete — ChatGPT has more world knowledge behind it. But for questions about your own documents, private AI answers more precisely because it searches the real source instead of guessing.</p>
			</details>
			<details class="faq-item">
				<summary>Can I try it before committing to anything?</summary>
				<p>Yes. We start with a concrete, narrow case using your own documents, measurable within weeks, before talking about anything bigger.</p>
			</details>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="block">
		<div class="final-cta">
			<div>
				<h2>Let's see it with your data</h2>
				<p>A 30-minute call to figure out which case makes sense to start with in your company.</p>
			</div>
			<a class="cta" href="/en/contact">Book a call</a>
		</div>
	</section>

	<BackLink lang="en" />
</Layout>

<style>
	.risk-grid.cols-2 {
		grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
		max-width: 720px;
	}
	.compare-grid {
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.5rem;
		margin-top: 1.5rem;
	}
	.compare-row {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;
		gap: 1rem;
		padding: 0.9rem 1.1rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--border);
		border-radius: 12px;
		background: var(--card);
		font-size: 0.88rem;
		line-height: 1.5;
	}
	.compare-header {
		background: transparent;
		border: none;
		padding: 0 1.1rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		color: var(--muted);
		font-size: 0.8rem;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		letter-spacing: 0.03em;
	}
	.compare-label {
		font-weight: 700;
	}
	@media (max-width: 640px) {
		.compare-row {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
			gap: 0.35rem;
		}
		.compare-header {
			display: none;
		}
		.compare-row:not(.compare-header) span:not(.compare-label)::before {
			content: attr(data-label) ": ";
			font-weight: 700;
			color: var(--muted);
		}
	}
</style>

<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
	"@context": "https://schema.org",
	"@type": "FAQPage",
	mainEntity: [
		{ "@type": "Question", name: "Is this the same as using ChatGPT Enterprise or Microsoft Copilot?", acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: "No. Those tools still process your data in the provider's cloud, even under enterprise contracts. Private AI runs both the model and the search inside your own infrastructure — there's no data transfer to a third party at any point." } },
		{ "@type": "Question", name: "Do I need powerful servers of my own?", acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: "It depends on document volume and concurrent users. A pilot with a few hundred documents runs on moderate hardware, no dedicated GPU required. We size the exact hardware for your case before starting." } },
		{ "@type": "Question", name: "Where exactly does the server get installed?", acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: "Inside your network — in your own offices or your datacenter if you already have one. It's not a virtual machine in a third party's cloud with extra locks on it: it's physical hardware under your control, connected only to your internal infrastructure." } },
		{ "@type": "Question", name: "Does it stop working if the internet goes down?", acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: "No, once deployed. The model and the search run inside your local network, so availability depends on your own infrastructure, not on an external service." } },
		{ "@type": "Question", name: "Is it slower or worse than ChatGPT?", acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: "For general knowledge questions, it doesn't compete — ChatGPT has more world knowledge behind it. But for questions about your own documents, private AI answers more precisely because it searches the real source instead of guessing." } },
		{ "@type": "Question", name: "Can I try it before committing to anything?", acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: "Yes. We start with a concrete, narrow case using your own documents, measurable within weeks, before talking about anything bigger." } },
	],
})} />
